WEBVTT

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.840
That was fun.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.660
I wonder if there are spy groups 
like that in Japan, too.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.360
Would they pretend to be normal
corporations and take new hires?

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.470
Well, you'd probably have to be smart to get in.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.050
What's wrong?

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.010
You know...

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.090
I should've gotten the 
caramel nut flavor instead.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.550
You...

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.960
You ate a ton of the 
plum and bonito flakes flavor!

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.240
But there are just so many 
temptations at a movie theater.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.050
I wanted to try the waffles and doughnuts, too.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.700
I get it!

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.320
Wanna hit up a place that's got waffles, then?

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:03.620
Yeah!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.460
<b>Skip Road</b>

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:09.630
Thank you.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:10.920
Bye.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.410
Yeah, see you.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.380
The green tea tart with whipped 
cream looked good, too.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.530
Tsumugi-chan?

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:37.990
Who's that?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:12.460
<b>A Day Off and Special Doughnuts</b>

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.880
Hey, where are we going next?

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.930
Just come with me.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.020
Please Charge

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.610
I'm out of battery.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.480
Want an ice pop?

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.810
Can I?

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.400
Yay!

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.590
I'm super aggro now, you know.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.480
But it's cold and tasty, right?

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.240
Yeah, thanks!

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.560
<b>Fluffy Bakes</b>

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:48.380
Have these, too.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.130
Okay!

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.100
She shouldn't eat all that at once!

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.060
So crunchy!

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.000
You're eating everything else I give you,

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.030
so why didn't you want the doughnuts?

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.950
Doughnuts are just... difficult for a snack.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.680
Difficult?

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.150
They make you full, right?

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.140
You shouldn't eat too much.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.420
You want one, too?

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:34.580
'Kay!

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.260
No!

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.230
Kotori-chan?

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:49.990
Hey!

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.410
Sorry I'm late!

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:54.990
Daddy!

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:56.110
Sensei?

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:58.740
Huh? What are you doing here?

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:03.850
Th-This man... k-kidnapped... Tsumugi-chan!

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:04.800
Kidnapped?

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.500
A-And he offered her a cigarette!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.160
Chocolate?

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.930
I want one, too!

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.520
He kidnapped Tsumugi?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.480
Him?

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.970
U-Um, do you know him?

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.890
He's a high school classmate of mine.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.220
His name's Yagi.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.720
We're friends.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:40.040
When I can't get her to 
kindergarten or a sitter,

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:43.840
I sometimes ask him to look after Tsumugi.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.920
I... I see.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:51.740
Splash!

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.930
Sensei... has friends.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.120
What?

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.790
Oh, it's nothing.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.060
Sorry.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.390
I had to mediate a fight between 
some students, and it ran long.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:10.400
Doesn't bother me. I'm not doing 
anything during lunchtime.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.510
Tsumugi's gotten bigger again.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.170
Yeah.

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:17.680
She was using some weird teenage slang.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:18.920
"Aggro," was it?

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.110
That's right.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.510
She learns it at her kindergarten.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.360
You think she'll end up becoming a gyaru?

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:29.210
No, she's probably just using it 
because she thinks it's funny.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.680
She's gonna keep getting bigger,

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.600
and looking more like her mother.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:42.060
Won't be long before she 
brings home a boyfriend home.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.420
Stop it, really.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:55.050
Tsumugi-chan, you were saying earlier 
that doughnuts were difficult.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.340
Do you like doughnuts?

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.250
I don't eat them that much.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.210
That's the girl from Megumi?

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.730
I've been there for lunch a few 
times, but I've never seen her.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.880
She's in school during lunch.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.590
The class where you're an assistant teacher?

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.280
Yeah. She's teaching me to cook.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.060
You're cooking, huh?

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.280
I make a lot of stuff at home, too.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:26.730
Lately I've made Hamburg steak 
and stuffed green peppers.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.070
Yeah?

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.030
Tsumugi likes her, too.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.160
It's a big help.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.490
Oh, thank you too, Yagi.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.320
Don't say it like you just remembered.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.000
Going to the bathroom?

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.810
No.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:47.580
Sensei, can we make doughnuts?

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:51.340
Doughnuts?

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.760
Doughnuts?!

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.960
You can <i>make</i> doughnuts?!

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:56.020
Yes.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.140
Let's have them for lunch tomorrow.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.020
I'll ask my mom for the recipe.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.720
Why this, all of a sudden?

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:06.360
Tsumugi said she resists eating doughnuts.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.370
Why'd you tell him?

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:11.210
Tsumugi...

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.350
Did you want to eat doughnuts?

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.040
Let's do it.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:28.890
Okay!

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:30.760
Yay!

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.830
Yay! Doughnuts!

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:33.970
Looks like he's having fun.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:39.890
Magi-Magic Magi-Girl Magi-Girl!

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:43.340
The arcade was fun today, 
wasn't it, Yagi-chan?

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:45.070
You went to the arcade?

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:45.960
Yup!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:46.880
I see.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.110
That's nice.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:50.440
You get to eat doughnuts tomorrow, huh?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.190
Yup.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.050
Have you made fried foods before?

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.340
No, not yet.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.740
Watch the temperature of the oil.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:01.450
Take care.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.410
Thanks.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.260
Oh, Yagi-chan!

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:06.710
This one's yours!

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.710
I don't need sparkling eyes like that.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.720
<b>Butcher</b>

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.810
Croquettes here! Piping hot and fresh!

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:30.740
Sizzly!

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.850
Want a croquette?

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:35.510
Yeah!

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.290
<b>Megumi</b>

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:54.030
Good morning.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:56.000
Good morning!

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.100
Good morning!

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:01.280
I was surprised at how early 
you wanted us here.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:05.120
The dough needs time to rise, 
so it does take a while.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:07.440
Are doughnuts difficult?

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:08.770
Don't worry.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:13.400
<b><i>Sugar</i></b>

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:14.440
<b>Strong Flour</b>

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:14.440
<b>Weak Flour</b>

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:14.440
<b>Dry
Yeast</b>

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.320
150 grams of weak flour,

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:13.560
150 grams of strong flour,

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.440
6 grams of dry yeast,

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.780
<b>Milk</b>

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.780
<b>Butter</b>

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.180
9 grams of granulated sugar,

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:18.780
and 3 grams of salt.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.650
Those are the ingredients in group A.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:26.020
Group B is one egg, 100 milliliters 
of milk, and 30 grams of butter.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:28.290
Oh, you divide them into classes?

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:35.130
Put all the ingredients in A 
into a bowl and mix thoroughly,

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:38.540
then mix everything in B and double-boil it.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:42.630
Add B to A, then mix.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.700
Once it all comes together,

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:47.600
move it to a surface you've 
dusted with strong flour.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:53.060
Knead the dough, working in the butter 
we've warmed to room temperature.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.610
Like this?

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.070
Looks good.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:05.800
How long do I do this?

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.820
Um... Eight minutes or so?

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.380
Eight minutes?

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:11.710
That's quite a while.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:12.840
Let's take turns.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:13.460
My turn!

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:15.920
I've stored up my power!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.250
Tsumugi-chan, that's dangerous!

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.220
Okay, take care of it.

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:25.900
I'll knead it!

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:28.710
Here we go.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.360
It's sticky.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.980
Shall we dust our hands?

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:44.160
Switch!

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.240
Leave it to me!

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:51.330
Once it forms a thin film like this 
that doesn't rip, it's ready.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:54.650
Put the dough in a bowl 
coated with vegetable oil,

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:57.420
then double-boil it for an hour 
or so to let the dough rise.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:00.010
We've got lots of time.

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:02.590
I know.

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:08.550
Sensei, you don't have to clean.

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:12.030
No, you always help us out so much. 
It's the least I can do.

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:12.940
Oh, yeah!

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:15.990
I've got a present for you, Kotori-chan!

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:21.180
I took these with Yagi-chan 
yesterday at the arcade!

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:25.760
Guess what? There was this big noise 
at the arcade going "boom boom"!

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.530
It went super-duper "boom"!

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:32.040
I told Yagi-chan to get me a 
stuffed animal, and he couldn't!

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:35.400
It was kind of amazing.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:44.200
Um, is it okay to leave 
Yagi-san with Tsumugi-chan?

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.010
Oh, sure.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.720
I think it's a good idea for her to be 
able to go wild once in a while.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.630
I'm, well...

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:54.060
I'm too normal.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.250
I don't know how to go wild.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.260
Yagi's good at that.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:06.650
They do say that both bad men 
and sweet sweets are alluring, but...

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.890
Oh, no, Yagi might look like a bad guy,

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:11.760
but he's not...

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:13.580
But what's wrong with being normal?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.910
Normal, plain sweets that aren't too sweet...

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:19.710
They're good, too!

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.250
Thank you!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.210
It plumped up!

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.720
Push down on the dough to let the gas out,

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:34.720
then cut into ten parts and roll them into balls.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.050
Let them rest for a while,

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.810
then push down on them,

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.720
forming them into a doughnut shape 
while making the hole bigger.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.780
Tsumugi, want to try it, too?

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:48.990
I do!

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:53.000
I'm gonna make the hole small!

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:57.710
The hole might disappear when it puffs up.

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.720
It's an experiment, so it's okay!

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.160
Really?

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:04.940
Well, let's see how it turns out.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:08.980
Now we let them rise for another hour.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:10.150
I see.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.670
What should I clean next?

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:15.580
The ceiling?

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:16.400
Sensei...

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:18.140
Yes? Should I clean the ceiling?

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:21.230
I came up with a way to spend the time!

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.020
Oh?

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:30.400
Daddy, put the money in first!

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.360
Ah, I see.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:33.200
<i>Choose your background!</i>

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:38.040
Normal      Passion      Cute      Cool

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.320
Huh? What?

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.930
How do I choose?

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:38.060
You do this, Daddy!

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:40.730
<i>Is this one okay?</i>

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:43.150
Uh... Yes!

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:44.290
You push the button.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:48.710
<i>Here we go! 3, 2...</i>

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.360
Go ahead!

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:50.920
We're back!

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.470
Welcome back.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.820
Look! It's super cute!

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:57.890
It sure is!

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.660
Tsumugi did almost all of it for me.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.400
There was still the "boom boom" 
noise at the arcade!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.590
It was super loud!

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:09.000
Yeah. It was.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.150
Right?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.820
That's nice.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:14.310
Yeah!

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.320
Okay!

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:32.700
You can do it, Daddy!

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.590
Y-You can do it!

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.050
R-Right!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.430
Here I go.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:50.860
Sizzly!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.380
Shall we turn them over now?

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:08.080
Okay.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:13.090
It's burnt!

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:14.240
What do we do?

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.770
Sensei, take it out of the oil!

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:16.710
Okay!

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:18.600
It fell!

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:20.650
Sensei, take it out, quick!

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:21.640
R-Right!

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.400
Chocolate?

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.020
Burnt doughnuts...

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.880
It's still undercooked inside.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:38.170
Maybe the oil was too hot.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:40.280
Temperature...

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:42.730
Wait a second.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:48.190
I'm sorry!

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:52.380
It said the temperature needed to be 
between 170 and 180 degrees Celsius.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.040
So it burned because it was too hot.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:58.200
Are these yummy?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.920
No, they're not.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:03.020
Sorry, Tsumugi.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.920
We did all this work,

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:09.570
but Daddy screwed up at the last step.

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:10.710
I'm really sorry.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:14.600
Doughnuts really are difficult.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.400
Yeah.

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:19.660
It was all going so well until now...

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:21.290
We're not done yet.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.850
We still have six left.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.940
That's right.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.290
My doughnut is still there!

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:33.280
This time, let's check the temperature 
of the oil before we fry them.

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.960
Let's check carefully!

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:35.850
Yup.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:37.580
Okay, one more time!

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:54.980
Go ahead.

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.990
You can do it, Daddy!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.220
Yeah!

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:02.950
Here I go.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:16.920
There.

00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:32.060
Shall we turn them over now?

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:33.270
Okay.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.380
We did it!

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:47.900
They're done!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.130
They're doughnuts, Daddy!

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:53.030
Yeah!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.230
They're really doughnuts!

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.440
Yeah!

00:19:57.440 --> 00:20:00.540
Let's add the honey sugar glaze 
while they're still hot.

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:03.210
H-Honey sugar... g-glaze?

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.800
And the double-boiled chocolate...

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:05.720
Chocolate?!

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:13.730
Let's eat!

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.650
It's crispy and fluffy!

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:29.330
They taste great plain, too.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:33.550
I bet if you added a salad, 
they'd make a great breakfast!

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.630
The one I made, like, has no hole!

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:43.580
It's a doughnut with no hole! Isn't that funny?

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:47.260
So it closed up after all, huh?

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.290
Argh! I'll eat you!

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:53.270
Is it good, Tsumugi?

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:57.620
I'm busy with this chocolate stuff right now.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:59.770
That's bad manners!

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:03.580
I thought that doughnuts were difficult,

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:09.900
'cause I didn't know if they 
were a snack or a meal.

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:12.650
Difficult, huh?

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.790
But from now on,

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:18.630
I know they're a happy thing that I eat

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.800
on my days off with Daddy!

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:34.810
Lots of happy things happened today, 
didn't they, Tsumugi-chan?

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:36.280
Yeah!

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:39.740
I'm gonna eat you! I'm gonna eat you!

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.300
A happy thing...

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:45.960
I'm gonna eat you!

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:47.380
I'm gonna eat you!
